    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "ASP.NET Core is a cross-platform, high-performance, open-source framework for building modern, cloud-based, Internet-connected applications. The latest version right now is ASP.NET Core 10.0."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "ASP.NET Core vs .NET Core"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "The differences between **ASP.NET Core and .NET Core** are as follows:"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "data": {
        "headers": [
          "ASP.NET Core",
          ".NET Core"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "ASP.NET Core is a collection of libraries that builds a web framework. This framework is used to create websites and web apps including mobile apps and IoT apps.",
            ""
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "ASP.NET Core 1.x-2.x – ASP.NET Core can be used on both .NET Core and the .NET Framework. This also means that an ASP.NET Core application is also a .NET Core application or a .NET Framework application."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "ASP.NET Core 3.x – depends on .NET Core and can no longer be used on .NET Framework."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Download the latest version .NET from Microsoft website, [link is here](https://dotnet.microsoft.com/en-us/download)."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "data": {
        "src": "https://www.yogihosting.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/aspnet-core.png \"ASP.NET Core\"",
        "alt": "aspnet core",
        "caption": null
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**ASP.NET** Core provides the following benefits:"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "A unified approach for building web UI and web APIs which is Architected for testability."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Razor Pages makes coding page-focused scenarios easier and more productive.",
          "***Platform Independent*** i.e. ability to develop and run on Windows, macOS, and Linux."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Integration of modern, client-side frameworks like React, Angular, *jQuery*, Bootstrap & Vue.js",
          "A cloud-ready, environment-based configuration system."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Built-in** **dependency injection** for making loosely coupled designs.",
          "A lightweight, high-performance, and modular HTTP request pipeline."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Ability to host on IIS, Nginx, Apache, Docker, or self-host in your own process."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Audience"
      }
    },
